{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Payment Service API","description":"Stripe card payments. Errors are returned as application/problem+json.","version":"v1"},"servers":[{"url":"/","description":"Current host"}],"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"tags":[{"name":"Payments","description":"Card payments through Stripe"}],"paths":{"/webhooks/flutterwave":{"post":{"tags":["flutterwave-webhook-controller"],"operationId":"receive","parameters":[{"name":"verif-hash","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"200":{"description":"OK"}}}},"/api/v1/payments/webhook":{"post":{"tags":["Payments"],"summary":"Stripe webhook (called by Stripe, public)","description":"Receives `payment_intent.succeeded` / `payment_intent.payment_failed`, updates the payment and publishes `payment.completed` / `payment.failed`. Not meant to be called manually — the `Stripe-Signature` header is verified with STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET. To test locally: `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8080/api/v1/payments/webhook`.","operationId":"handleWebhook","parameters":[{"name":"Stripe-Signature","in":"header","description":"Signature header set by Stripe","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Event processed","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"Missing or invalid Stripe signature","content":{"*/*":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ProblemDetail"}}}}},"security":[]}},"/api/v1/payments/create-order":{"post":{"tags":["Payments"],"summary":"Create a Stripe payment order","description":"Creates a Stripe PaymentIntent in USD for one of **your own** accounts. Use the returned `clientSecret` and `stripePublishableKey` with Stripe.js / Stripe Elements on the frontend to collect the card. The final result arrives through the webhoo